<div class="row">
    <p class="lead">
        >>  The future of the invisible rail system for teeth began in 1998  <<
    </p>

    <p>
        The goal was to stop using dental braces, wires and glue for teeth correction to let the user <br />

        go through their normal daily oral hygiene procedure. <br />

        Often caries and periodontal disease limit the effects of conventional dental braces <br />

        in orthodontics. <br />
        
        Using the Clear-Aligner System of Prof. Dr. TaeWeon Kim this goal could be achieved! <br />

        He introduced his break through technology in 1998: using thin plastic rails, which <br />

        could be put over the teeth, he was able to move individual teeth or groups into <br />

